# Expression Bodies for Single-Return Methods

Use expression body syntax (`=>`) for methods and functions that only return a value.

## Widget build() Methods

```dart
// BAD - unnecessary braces and return keyword
@override
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  return Container();
}

// GOOD - expression body
@override
Widget build(BuildContext context) => Container();
```

## Getters

```dart
// BAD
String get fullName {
  return '$firstName $lastName';
}

// GOOD
String get fullName => '$firstName $lastName';
```

## Simple Methods

```dart
// BAD
int calculateTotal() {
  return price * quantity;
}

// GOOD
int calculateTotal() => price * quantity;
```

## When NOT to Use Expression Bodies

Use block bodies when:
- Method has multiple statements
- Method needs local variables
- Logic is complex enough to benefit from multi-line formatting

```dart
// Block body is appropriate here
Future<void> fetchData() async {
  final response = await api.get('/data');
  state = AsyncData(response.data);
}
```
